# GQuay Tier 1 secrets.
#
# These cannot live in GitHub. The REST API lists Actions *secrets* without
# revealing their values — by design, and only a workflow runtime can decrypt
# one. The Router is a standalone process, not an Actions job, so a value it
# cannot read back is a value it cannot use. Actions *Variables* are different
# and are read live; see docs/06-configuration.md for the four-tier split.
#
# Copy to .env and chmod 600.

# ── Claude ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Use a Console API key with its own billing and spend controls. A Max-plan
# OAuth token works for personal automation, but this pipeline routes other
# people's requests through one person's seat on shared infrastructure — which
# is exactly the case that calls for an API key or a Team plan.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── GitHub App ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Prefer github.private_key_path in router.yml. This is the inline alternative.
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----"

# The webhook HMAC secret. Must be known before any GitHub call is trusted.
GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Hook Bus ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bearer for the loopback hook listener. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
HOOK_BUS_TOKEN=

# ── Teams ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Power Automate Workflows trigger URL. The `sig` query parameter is a
# credential, so treat the entire URL as one. Hooks never see this — only the
# Hook Bus holds it.
TEAMS_WORKFLOW_URL=

# ── Dispatch workers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One per dispatch target, matching its worker_token_env in router.yml.
GQUAY_WORKER_TOKEN_KINGSPAN=

# ── Optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GQUAY_LOG_LEVEL=info
# GQUAY_CONFIG=/etc/gquay/router.yml
